## OpenSpec-governed changes

- Use `$govern-openspec-context` for non-trivial project changes and for resuming any
  active OpenSpec change.
- At startup, read `openspec/project-context.md`, enumerate changes with OpenSpec JSON,
  and reconcile the selected change's artifacts and `handoff.md` with repository state.
- Let the governance skill classify risk and automatically compose the generated
  OpenSpec action skills; do not require the user to invoke every lifecycle phase.
- Keep exactly one writer and one exclusive implementation branch/worktree per active
  change. Parallel work must use separate, non-overlapping changes and branches.
- Update `handoff.md` at task boundaries and before cross-session handoff. Use real Git
  checkpoint commits and structured verification results; never store secrets or
  credentials in OpenSpec artifacts.
- For branch/PR delivery, archive after merge unless the user explicitly selects local
  branch archive.
<!-- govern-openspec-context:end -->
